OpenRGB (private lighting engine)
  Author: Adam Honse (CalcProgrammer1) and contributors
  https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later
  On Windows, ChromaFlow installs OpenRGB under
  Program Files\ChromaFlow\engine\OpenRGB\ (or %LOCALAPPDATA%\chromaflow\engine)
  as a private SDK server on 127.0.0.1:6742 — a separate process, not a
  standalone user app (no Start Menu shortcut). On Linux Mint the .deb may ship
  OpenRGB.AppImage under /usr/libexec/chromaflow/. Detector identity for the
  lighting gap list is in data/openrgb-device-index.csv (GPL index of facts; not
  controller source). Refresh: `python3 scripts/agent-run.py fetch-openrgb-device-index`.

